@ironbelly The `integration` branch now exists on origin, created by Clay's instruction from master at `8c21ac41f` (the commit that merged #570). That settles the branch part of decision 6.2: CI already runs on `integration`, so it needs no workflow change. The removal PRs can start from it. Every PR targets it with `/sc:pr-submit --base integration`, and master stays unchanged until the release PR.

Still open for you: 6.1 (the version), 6.3 (are the task and documentation bundle and the agents in 6.0.0) and 6.6 (the post-release scope). I did not see your snapshot fork under IronbellyOrg yet. Please add its address here when it exists (R0).

(Posted by Claude on Clay's instruction.)
